-- ============================================================================
-- seeds/warcastle-tables.sql
--
-- Thirteen dummy table set-ups for WarCastle, one per area, until the real
-- ones are made (Grant, 21 Oct). Each was made in the scenario builder's
-- Set up > Tables (its Random set-up), so it opens in Play like any other:
-- the table and six terrain features, with no deployment (the attack sets
-- that). Every table has strategic locations (2 to 4 markers); tables 4, 6,
-- 7 and 13 also have a special feature. They are named "Dummy N: ..." so
-- they're easy to spot and replace in Set up > Tables.
--
-- Run in the Supabase SQL editor, after seeds/warcastle.sql. It adds the
-- scenarios to the WarCastle event and sets them as Tables 1 to 13. Then
-- re-run seeds/warcastle-test.sql to copy them into WarCastle (test).
--
-- Safe to run again: the scenarios keep their ids, so a re-run puts them
-- back as they were and sets them on their tables again (and replaces the
-- first version of this seed's dummies).
-- ============================================================================

